            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0929" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.796/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Poindexter</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-25T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                                1928—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Your 4, January 21, 1 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The phrase “foreign interests” is intended to cover all interests in Peru
                        not American or Peruvian.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The American interests referred to in the Department’s 4, January 19, 3
                        p.m., are the Keystone and Huff-Daland Dusters, who are connected with
                        Hayden Stone (Financial) and Pan American Airways, and possibly eventually
                        others.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Give all possible and proper support to Woolman.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
